INT. STRIKE ZONE LANES - OFFICE - NIGHT

A defunct bowling alley. Dead pinsetters hulk in the dark beyond the glass. A steel desk. A cassette recorder on the blotter. A rotary phone, unplugged.

Nothing moves.

A key turns. The door sticks, then gives. INSPECTOR NELL AKINTOLA, 50s, raincoat, flat shoes, a paper evidence bag under her arm, steps in and shakes water from her hair.

She sets the bag on the desk. Presses PLAY on the recorder.

NELL (V.O.)
(tape, tinny)
Tuesday. Strike Zone. Owner says he never left the shift.

NELL
He did.

NELL (V.O.)
(tape)
Receipts say otherwise. Parking stub at the Harbour Hotel, ten fifteen.

NELL
Ten fourteen, actually.

NELL (V.O.)
(tape)
Lane eleven. The foul line. Something under the tape.

NELL
Three keys on a ring. Tagged. Not his.

NELL (V.O.)
(tape)
Ask about the night man.

NELL
Night man doesn't exist.

NELL (V.O.)
(tape)
So who signed the sheet?

NELL
That's what I'm asking, Nell.

She stops the tape. Rewinds a few seconds. Presses PLAY.

NELL (V.O.)
(tape)
Ask about the night man.

She nods. Takes out a pen. Writes on her palm. Switches off the recorder.

NELL
Night man.

She turns off the light and leaves. The door clicks shut.
